; A bare `any` type-choice arm in a NON-LAST position (`any / tstr`) is a GRACEFUL rejection in
; EVERY profile, at parse/IR time (wasm-independent): a bare `any` accepts every CBOR item, so any
; arm after it is unreachable dead code. The rejection message is "`any`
; arm makes later arms unreachable — move it last". A bare `any` arm IS supported in LAST position
; (`tests/robustness/choice_last_any_arm.cddl`), where the forced-backtracking
; dispatch falls a content-mismatched item through to the catch-all. A TAGGED `any` arm (`#6.n(any)`)
; is not a catch-all and may appear in any position. Formerly this shape panicked at an
; `Option::unwrap()` in intermediate/rust_type.rs; that was replaced with a blanket choice-arm
; rejection, later narrowed to this last-position rule. Surfaced by the recombination sweep
; (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
a = any / tstr
